    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1a1e4596bbd1eb35ccf35dc02c06684a60f1dd450255c6f9a25ced5517bf845c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The CUE and zeta calculations share a two-stage close-pair mechanism: after centering and separating the close pair from the remaining-root background, the nearby critical-point displacement is an even analytic function with leading order theta squared; pushing the quadratically vanishing small-gap density through that map yields an s-to-the-one-half boundary-distance density. After unfolding zeta zeros, the partial-fraction critical-point equation reproduces the polynomial equation's leading coefficients, so the zeta transfer is conditional on CUE spacing and conditioned-background statistics.",
